<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 15 March, from 44 BCE to 2019.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">44 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar assassinated on the Ides of March</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A group of senators led by Brutus and Cassius stabbed Caesar to death in the Curia of Pompey. Meant to save the Republic, the murder led to civil war and the rule of Augustus.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">493</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theoderic the Great kills Odoacer at Ravenna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long siege ended in a power-sharing agreement, Theoderic murdered Odoacer at a banquet. The Ostrogothic king then ruled Italy for over thirty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1493</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus returns to Spain from his first voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Columbus sailed into Palos, the port from which he had departed seven months earlier, with news of islands across the Atlantic. His voyages began lasting European contact with the Americas.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1564</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Akbar abolishes the jizya tax on non-Muslims</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mughal emperor ended the poll tax on non-Muslim subjects, part of a policy of conciliating the Hindu majority of his empire. Aurangzeb reimposed it in 1679.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1820</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maine becomes the 23rd US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Separated from Massachusetts, Maine entered the Union as a free state under the Missouri Compromise. Its admission balanced that of Missouri as a slave state.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1917</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Nicholas II abdicates</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Facing revolution in Petrograd and mutiny in the army, Nicholas II gave up the throne for himself and his son. Over three centuries of Romanov rule ended, and a Provisional Government took power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">2019</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 51 at two Christchurch mosques</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A white supremacist attacked worshippers at Friday prayers and livestreamed the killings. Within a month New Zealand's parliament banned most semi-automatic weapons.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></div></li></ol>
